{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011Ch1qub5hvsrVkK9UnkwMp", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I signed off with low confidence (0.4). I filed one bug, but the developer could not reproduce it, so it is unconfirmed, and two checks were not completed.\n\n**Possible bug (reported twice, \"could not reproduce\" both times):** on the main screen number pad, a third decimal digit seems to be accepted and rounded into the amount. Typing `.999` showed `$1`, and an earlier `.555` showed `$0.56`. Backspacing from `$1` gave `$0.99`, so the amount is probably still held with three decimals. I did not pin down exact steps that reproduce it reliably.\n\n**Checked and consistent:**\n- **Expense entry:** I entered 5.50 with the Food category. It was saved and shows under Today as Food, $5.5.\n- **Decimal key:** a leading `.` gives `$0.5`, and a second `.` is ignored.\n- **Budget sheet totals:** they show $65.5 spent, a $100 budget, 11 Nov to 04 Dec and 20 days remaining.\n- **Spending sum:** the $65.5 matches the starting data: groceries 40 plus rent 20 plus my 5.50.\n- **Breakdown dialog:** its arithmetic is correct.\n- **Rotation:** rotating to landscape and back lost nothing.\n\n**Not completed:**\n- I did not test the budget sheet with a different selected currency, because that would change app data.\n- I could not tell what the toolbar should show after a category is applied. It looked the same before and after, so I did not report it."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 961, "cache_read_input_tokens": 87331, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 961}, "output_tokens": 503, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool